WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.669
The Flow Part and the Bag Part display content items inside another content item.

00:00:05.669 --> 00:00:07.762
This video shows how they render:

00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:12.538
the shapes they produce, the templates and alternates that change their markup, and

00:00:12.538 --> 00:00:15.060
the templates of the widgets inside them.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.631
The Flow Part renders a shape named FlowPart.

00:00:22.631 --> 00:00:25.253
Its template loops through the widgets.

00:00:25.253 --> 00:00:28.866
It skips any item whose type is not a widget, and, for a

00:00:28.866 --> 00:00:33.410
securable type, any widget that the current user is not allowed to view.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.180
Each remaining widget is built with the display type of the item that

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.163
holds the Flow, such as Detail.

00:00:40.163 --> 00:00:44.130
Its shape is Widget, and one of its alternates, a more specific name

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:48.150
that a template can target, is named after the widget's content type.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.917
When a widget has Flow metadata, the template adds CSS classes to its

00:00:53.917 --> 00:01:00.540
shape for the type, the alignment and the size, such as widget-paragraph and widget-size-100.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:11.333
To change how Paragraph widgets render, add Widget-Paragraph.liquid to the Views folder of your theme.

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:14.080
This is the template of The Blog Theme:

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:19.880
an article element whose class attribute is Model.Classes, around the rendered paragraph.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:25.011
In a file name, a dash stands for two underscores in the shape type.

00:01:25.011 --> 00:01:30.634
A dot before the extension adds a display type, so Widget-Paragraph.Summary.liquid is the

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:33.180
Summary version of the same template.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:37.091
A widget can have these alignment and size classes.

00:01:37.091 --> 00:01:41.750
Print Model.Classes in your own template to keep them, as The Blog Theme does.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.584
The Bag Part renders a shape named BagPart.

00:01:48.584 --> 00:01:52.830
Its template builds each contained item with the Display Type of the part

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:56.270
settings, and with Summary when that setting has no value.

00:01:57.883 --> 00:02:01.089
This is the editor of the Landing Page content type.

00:02:01.089 --> 00:02:04.627
A Bag Part can be named, so one type can hold several, and

00:02:04.627 --> 00:02:07.723
Landing Page has named Bag Parts such as Services.

00:02:08.176 --> 00:02:10.825
Edit the Services part to see its settings.

00:02:10.825 --> 00:02:15.205
Display Type has the placeholder Summary, and its hint says that Summary is

00:02:15.205 --> 00:02:18.016
the default for rendering the contained items.

00:02:19.616 --> 00:02:22.983
The shape of each item depends on its content type.

00:02:22.983 --> 00:02:27.649
A Paragraph widget has the Widget stereotype, so its shape is Widget, and

00:02:27.649 --> 00:02:31.606
with Summary its template is Widget-Paragraph.Summary.liquid.

00:02:31.606 --> 00:02:35.386
A Service item has no stereotype, so its shape is Content.

00:02:36.136 --> 00:02:41.439
Widget-Paragraph.liquid targets the Detail display type, so it does not apply to a

00:02:41.439 --> 00:02:43.609
Bag Part that renders Summary.

00:02:43.609 --> 00:02:47.706
Name the template for the display type that the Bag Part uses.

00:02:51.906 --> 00:02:54.511
The part shapes have alternates too.

00:02:54.511 --> 00:03:03.195
LandingPage-BagPart.liquid targets the Bag Parts of the type LandingPage, and LandingPage-Services.liquid only the one named Services.

00:03:03.195 --> 00:03:05.366
Flow Parts work the same way.

00:03:06.116 --> 00:03:10.800
By default, a Flow Part displays only in the Detail display type, while

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.024
a Bag Part displays in both Detail and Summary.

00:03:14.024 --> 00:03:17.856
The display driver of each part declares these locations.

00:03:18.606 --> 00:03:24.289
An empty Flow or Bag renders as FlowPart_Empty or BagPart_Empty, and the Flows

00:03:24.289 --> 00:03:27.265
module ships empty templates for them.

00:03:27.265 --> 00:03:31.662
A rule in a placement file can set the shape to FlowPart to

00:03:31.662 --> 00:03:33.556
use the full template.

00:03:34.306 --> 00:03:41.509
If you replace FlowPart.cshtml, your template takes over the checks and the classes of the original.

00:03:41.509 --> 00:03:47.216
The Default Theme does this, with a copy whose section also has the row class.

00:03:51.416 --> 00:03:57.545
A content template can skip the part shape and read a named Bag Part directly.

00:03:57.545 --> 00:04:05.716
In Liquid, Model.ContentItem.Content.Services.ContentItems lists the items of the Bag Part named Services.

00:04:06.466 --> 00:04:10.772
The landing page template of the Agency recipe does this.

00:04:10.772 --> 00:04:17.948
It calls shape_build_display for each service, renders only its HtmlBodyPart with shape_render, and

00:04:17.948 --> 00:04:20.886
writes the surrounding markup itself.

00:04:25.089 --> 00:04:29.300
To see which template renders a shape, open Settings, Debugging.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:32.909
The page has the option Write shape debug information.

00:04:33.365 --> 00:04:35.261
Check the option, and save.

00:04:35.261 --> 00:04:39.798
The site then wraps the rendered shapes in HTML comments, and keeps doing

00:04:39.798 --> 00:04:41.865
so until you clear the option.

00:04:43.465 --> 00:04:48.777
In the page source, each comment names the shape type and the template that rendered it.

00:04:48.777 --> 00:04:54.088
Outside the Production environment, the console_log filter also prints a shape, with its

00:04:54.088 --> 00:04:56.405
alternates, to the browser console.

00:04:58.405 --> 00:05:02.492
A template named after the part, the content type or the widget, with

00:05:02.492 --> 00:05:06.088
the display type added, changes how a Flow or a Bag renders.

00:05:06.088 --> 00:05:07.505
Thanks for watching.

